      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s say we have two apexes each of which uses a different version of the same sdk module.\n\napex { name: \"apex1\", java_libs: [\"mylib\"], uses_sdks: [\"mysdk#1\"]}\napex { name: \"apex2\", java_libs: [\"mylib\"], uses_sdks: [\"mysdk#2\"]}\njava_library { name: \"mylib\", libs: [\"sdkmember\"]}\nsdk { name: [\"mysdk\"], java_libs: [\"sdkmember\"] }\n\nwhen mylib is built for apex1, it should link against version 1 snapshot of sdkmember, while it is built for apex2, it should link against version 2 snapshot of sdkmember.\n\nIn order for each of the versioned prebuilt libraries (sdkmember@mysdk#1, sdkmember@mysdk#2) to replace the source built library (sdkmember) differently depending on which apex they are in, the source built one should also be mutated for the apexes. Otherwise, replacing sdkmember with sdkmember@mysdk#1 for the apex1 would affect apex2 as well.",
